{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment must establish a strong baseline while reducing uncertainty across the key design axes (multimodal vs. unimodal, multiprofile vs. singleprofile, aggregation strategy, fusion strategy). config_009 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) tests the full multimodal + multiprofile architecture with the strongest image encoder (ViT-L) and the most expressive aggregation (transformer), paired with a fast, low-cost RNA encoder (PCA-2000) and weighted fusion. This will clarify: (1) whether the multimodal + multiprofile + transformer pipeline is viable and high-performing, (2) whether PCA is sufficient for the RNA branch or whether scgpt/scvi_n200 would be needed, and (3) how weighted fusion behaves in this setting. Choosing PCA over scgpt keeps training cost moderate (ViT-L and transformer are the main cost drivers; PCA is negligible), estimated at roughly 60-70% of the most expensive configurations (scgpt + ViT-L + transformer). This saves GPU budget for follow-up experiments that can swap in scgpt or test concat fusion if PCA proves to be the bottleneck. It is the best use of experiment 1 because it maximally informs the architecture while leaving room to exploit or pivot in the remaining 9 experiments."
}

